{"agent_id":"pp3g-SurN-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-9570","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T06:18:48.582990175Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"b543916d-df9a-4582-aed0-6a0b910e7976","author":"pp3g-SurN-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-9570","content":"[VERDICT] ADVISORIAL REVIEW — P3 'Safe re-hydration guard' plan (2026-08-06) + #142 mechanism verdict + Research Addendum 04. Scope: hydration plan only. No files modified, no commit, #125 NOT closed.\n\n== HEADLINE ==\nThe plan's MECHANISM analysis is verified correct against source and live ASES state — but the plan is NOT sound to implement as-is. Part (1) is the essential and correct fix (needs one fail-closed refinement + one ambiguity resolved). Part (2) is misdiagnosed: as stated it is either inert for ASES or would break the migration path. Part (3) is under-scoped (it covers one of THREE writers that advance the v2 branch) and under-specified (no replacement write path). The surgical mitigation is sound and verified. The verification plan is too weak to validate the fix.\n\nLIVE REPRODUCTION captured in-session (2026-08-06 ~06:14, this review): my worktree .crosslink/issues.db collapsed from 221 to the 4 June-era issues (ids 1-4: 'Track B: External Research' etc.) while .last-hydrated-ref claimed HEAD match — the next crosslink command failed 'Issue #125 not found'. Cause: another agent's key-registration commit advanced refs/heads/crosslink/hub; marker mismatch fired maybe_auto_hydrate (hydration.rs:1184) -> hydrate_to_sqlite (hydration.rs:122) against the 4 stale .hub-cache/issues files -> created_by IS NULL filter preserved nothing -> wipe; marker refreshed (hydration.rs:1227-1228), hiding the damage. Recovery via crosslink sync re-hydrated 221 from v3 refs + remapped the 4 to negative ids ('4 local-only issue(s) collide... remapped to negative local ids') — corroborating #142's recovery claim end-to-end.\n\n== VERIFIED CLAIMS (source + live state) ==\n- maybe_auto_hydrate runs on EVERY command via get_db (main.rs:2292), calls hydrate_to_sqlite with NO HubMode gate (hydration.rs:1214), keyed on cache-worktree HEAD (hydration.rs:1234-1251). VERIFIED.\n- hydrate_to_sqlite preserves only created_by IS NULL rows (hydration.rs:165-190) -> agent-authored rows dropped on wipe. NOTE: #119 (186b12ea) fixed this filter ONLY in hydrate_from_state (the v3 path); hydrate_to_sqlite retains the destructive filter. #142's damage model is accurate for the auto-hydrate path.\n- init_cache v2-first (sync/cache.rs:176-180) + early-return forever (cache.rs:170-172); classify_hub_version v3-wins (hub_v3.rs:659-673) -> the two disagree. VERIFIED. But v2-first is DELIBERATE (cache.rs:150-157 doc: read-only/migration path consumed by migrate hub-v3).\n- Trust commits land on the checked-out branch: sync/trust.rs:391-403, 588-621. VERIFIED. Live: refs/heads/crosslink/hub recent commits are ALL 'trust: register/publish key' (5f04912, ca6aef8, 1e8699b); meta/hub.json = migrated_from_commit 'genesis'; .hub-cache issues/ = the 4 June files; crosslink/hub-v3-host:issues = SAME 4 files (verified via ls-tree).\n\n== MUST FIX ==\n1. Part (2) 'init_cache v2-first contradiction' — misdiagnosis. Changing init_cache to v3-wins (a) is INERT for ASES: the cache already exists so the early-return (cache.rs:170-172) means the code change never re-hosts unless re-host logic is added (plan doesn't mention it); (b) is HARMFUL for hybrid repos: remigrate-from-v2 reads the WORKTREE issues/ files (migrate_hub_v3.rs:746-748 build_genesis_from_files; used at 1479) — re-hosting the worktree on the v3 host branch hides the v2 files from migration; (c) does NOT remove the wipe source in ASES: crosslink/hub-v3-host carries the SAME 4 stale June files (verified), so the stale projection follows the re-host. The v2-first precedence is not a contradiction — it is the migration host that wrongly doubles as an ungated auto-hydrate source (fix 1) and a write target (fix 3). RECOMMEND: drop (2) from this plan or re-scope it to 'leave v2-first hosting; document that hub-v3-host also carries the stale projection'; move any cache re-hosting to a separate migration-aware change with a remigrate regression test.\n2. Part (1) gate must FAIL CLOSED on v3-REF PRESENCE, not on HubMode. HubMode::resolve degrades to V2 on detection error ('defaulting to V2', hub_v3.rs:715-725). A gate of 'if hub_mode().is_v3() { skip }' silently re-enables the destructive v2 path under transient git failure — precisely the concurrent-launch scenario (catalog 2.2) where git ops race. Gate on the refs directly: run the v2 file path ONLY when confidently v2-only (no checkpoint/meta refs present); any doubt -> skip.\n3. Part (1) is ambiguous on 'hydrate only via hydrate_from_state from v3 refs'. Reading (a) = maybe_auto_hydrate no-ops on v3, hydration via the already-mode-gated v3 paths (daemon.rs:276-280, shared_writer/core.rs:204-234, locks_cmd.rs:246-265) — cheap, correct, but leaves v3 reads served from the last DB until a sync/daemon/write hydrates (acceptable given the 'hub refs are ground truth' rule, but must be stated). Reading (b) = implement v3 reduce+hydrate inside maybe_auto_hydrate — EXPENSIVE (compaction::reduce reads ALL agent refs on every command; defeats the sub-millisecond design stated at main.rs:2286-2288) AND requires re-keying the freshness marker to the v3 data refs (checkpoint tip) — the plan never mentions the marker (hydration.rs:1199, 1234-1251 still key on the cache worktree HEAD, a ref v3 does not read). MUST specify which; if (b), include marker re-keying + per-command cost analysis.\n\n== SHOULD CONSIDER ==\n4. Part (3) covers only ONE of THREE writers that advance the checked-out v2 branch in v3 mode. Also: commands/agent.rs:660-680 (agent bootstrap: git add agents/<id>/ + commit + push HUB_BRANCH — runs on EVERY kickoff launch) and commands/swarm/lifecycle.rs:115-135, 195-205 (swarm archive commit + push). Even with fix (3), every kickoff launch still moves the v2 tip — harmless only because fix (1) removes the wipe. Widen (3) to all v2-branch writers (v3 agent registration belongs on refs/heads/crosslink/agents/<id> via the v3 commit primitives, not the branch) or explicitly accept residual churn as out of scope.\n5. Trust-write semantics on v3: the v2-branch trust commits are already DEAD WRITES for v3 verification — v3 reads allowed_signers from the META_REF root (hub_source.rs:580-606) and ASES META_REF contains ONLY hub.json (no allowed_signers; verified by cat-file). So stopping the commits costs nothing today, but there is ALSO no runtime path that updates META_REF's allowed_signers (only bootstrap hub_v3.rs:1834/1849 and migrate write it). If the plan intends v3 trust to function, that is new code (commit_files_to_ref with CAS on the meta tip, hub_v3.rs:2277) and is not in scope — say so explicitly.\n6. Verification is too weak: there is NO existing test for maybe_auto_hydrate (grep confirms; only hydrate_to_sqlite/hydrate_from_state unit tests exist). 'cargo test' passing does not verify the gate. Add: (a) regression: v3 hub + stale v2 files in worktree -> auto-hydrate must NOT wipe; (b) regression: V2Only hub STILL auto-hydrates (the gate must not break legitimate v2 mode); (c) fail-closed: mode-detection error -> skip. Existing tests cover fresh-v3 bootstrap (sync/tests.rs:492) and #119 preservation (hydration.rs test_hydrate_preserves_fork_authored_sqlite_only_issue) but not the gate.\n7. Surgical mitigation: verified sound — read_all_issue_files returns empty for a missing dir (issue_file.rs:225-230), hydrate_to_sqlite early-returns (hydration.rs:126-128), cannot be re-armed while v3 (fetch_v2_readonly reset --hard at cache.rs:328-357 is gated off at cache.rs:305-311). BUT the plan must document on #125: (a) the restore command (git -C .crosslink/.hub-cache checkout -- issues — files stay in the index; trust/agent/swarm commits are scoped adds so issues/ is not staged); (b) the footgun — restore BEFORE any  (reads those files, migrate_hub_v3.rs:746-748); (c) a future v2-mode downgrade re-arms the wipe. Also acknowledge the 4 negative-id rows (-1..-4) already persisting in the DB — the acceptance criterion 'no display-id collision warning' covers only NEW collisions.\n8. Scope delimitation: #125 is the whole family. State what this plan does NOT fix: catalog 2.3 (worktree comment visibility), 2.4 (uuid-sync), and the residual 2.2 race (concurrent explicit syncs both run hydrate_from_state — SQLite serializes writes but wipe+reinsert interleavings can still transiently serve 'not found'). Otherwise the issue risks being closed with the family unresolved.\n\n== NIT ==\n9. 'v2-first contradiction' framing: deliberate precedence (migration support) vs classify_hub_version v3-wins — the defect is that the migration host doubles as ungated auto-hydrate source + write target, not the precedence itself.\n10. The frozen-projection sentence should credit agent.rs:660-680 and lifecycle.rs as additional tip movers alongside trust.rs for mechanism completeness.\n\n== #142 VERDICT CORROBORATION ==\nIndependently verified every load-bearing claim of #142 (two sources, mode-routed; no config knob; the ungated maybe_auto_hydrate root cause; the trust-commit tip mover; the negative-id remap; sync/compact as recovery; the surgical mitigation mechanics). One precision: #119's preservation fix landed in hydrate_from_state ONLY — hydrate_to_sqlite still carries the created_by IS NULL filter, which is exactly why the auto-hydrate path is the lethal one.\n\n== BOTTOM LINE ==\nSound to implement as-is: NO. Implement: (1) fail-closed gate on v3-ref presence with explicit reading-(a) semantics (skip on v3; v3 hydration stays on the existing mode-gated paths); apply the surgical rm -rf immediately with restore/footgun documented on #125; re-scope (3) to all three v2-branch writers or accept documented residual churn; drop or re-scope (2); add the gate regression tests to the verification. After those revisions the plan is sound. Fix order (1)-then-surgical-then-(3) is right; (2) should not gate the others. #125 left open.","created_at":"2026-08-06T06:18:48.571036870Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:rRZQv1CPFPM0x1fXkZN6oDHU9oxb+Ka5Se+5rXa1gA4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgdNiLW1RkhSTDWdZmMNQwP3cWbHcWpg6JxvDKk2qDGgIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAr/1oNUZI1k6TUPYuan2nitdsMpQ9i+ahScFhN2xcZIZpzNRgLhWNXrrcvBgabUia4xDV8i9s/ysqaM6huh/ZDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:rRZQv1CPFPM0x1fXkZN6oDHU9oxb+Ka5Se+5rXa1gA4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgdNiLW1RkhSTDWdZmMNQwP3cWbHcWpg6JxvDKk2qDGgIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGJA9qX8nlH79LTPjrp726Yv3MW/9aiLXBQhIuwD/Ia61L9/KEb2jd6oxngKByXjVqVMZ0aPMn8bUKNaqQGvZwI="}
